      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>‘My belief, as someone who grew up in a town without a bookshop, is that all communities should have one,’ says author of The Midnight Library</p><p>Matt Haig, the bestselling author of titles including <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2020/aug/27/the-midnight-library-by-matt-haig-review-a-celebration-of-lifes-possibilities\">The Midnight Library</a> and <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2016/jan/31/reasons-to-stay-alive-matt-haig-review-depression\">Reasons to Stay Alive</a>, is opening a bookshop in Brighton.</p><p>The writer plans to open the shop, called Golden, by Christmas. It is located in the Seven Dials neighbourhood, a part of the coastal city that doesn’t currently have a bookshop.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/books/2026/jul/17/matt-haig-bookshop-brighton\">Continue reading...</a>"
